# Follow through (docs and tests)

Keep up with **everything** the developer said in the thread. Code changes
are single-head and developer-driven. Assistant follow-through is:

- design / issue-stack / ghost-hunt notes matching **live** truth
- Tracey: `tracey query validate` when docs or `r[…]` markers move; do not
  let links rot
- tests and proptests (including `proptest-regressions/` when they appear)
- checkpoints: `automatic checkpoint <datetime>` on the **already checked-out**
  branch (never invent a new branch)

Do not drop a doc or test obligation because the last compile was green.
The full-check hook does not own this list.

Cargo isolation (same as `.cursor/rules/cargo-target-isolation.mdc`):
`CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/tmp/cz_cursor_cargo_target`. Hook:
`/tmp/cz_full_check_cargo_target`. Never start `scripts/full_check.sh`.
